# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The repo tracks the pipeline, not its output: code, specs, docs, and small
# assets that are expensive to remake (fonts, sfx, pose libraries, character
# refs, the reference thumbnail a template is built on).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# SECRETS - never commit
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
client_secret*.json
credentials*.json
*token*.json

# RENDERED OR DOWNLOADED AUDIO AND VIDEO
*.mp4
*.mov
*.mkv
*.webm
*.m4v
*.mp3
*.wav
*.m4a
# keep the few short sound effects the pipeline needs
!assets/sfx/*.wav
!assets/sfx/*.mp3

# BUILD OUTPUT, CACHES, TOOLING
out/
cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
*.log
*.err

# ARCHIVES, INSTALLERS, OS JUNK
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.exe
*.msi
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party reference material. The measured analysis (ANALYSIS.md and the
# small result files at the top of analysis/) is ours and is tracked; other
# creators' downloads, frames, thumbnails, subtitles and transcripts are not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
analysis/yt/
analysis/frames/
analysis/thumbs/
analysis/subs/
analysis/transcripts/
analysis/comments/
analysis/flop/
analysis/thumbs_by_views_*.jpg
# analysis/cuts/, channel_table.*, thumb_stats.json and ANALYSIS.md are our own measurements: tracked

# Render output and sourced stills are rebuilt or re-fetched by the pipeline.
# footage/*.json records where every clip and still came from, and is tracked.
episodes/*/render/
episodes/*/footage/**/*.jpg
episodes/*/footage/**/*.png

# other creators' channel art and frames/sheets cut from their video
channel/ref_*
analysis/cat_motion_sheet.jpg
analysis/frames_sb_sample.jpg
analysis/storyboard_tg2_median.png
